---
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="mt-16 border-t border-grid bg-panel">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-6 px-4 py-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:px-6">
    <div>
      <p class="font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-paper">{SITE_NAME}</p>
      <p class="term-label mt-2 text-dim">Market closes never · Past performance guarantees nothing</p>
      <ul class="term-label mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-[0.6875rem]">
        <li><a class="text-paper hover:text-phosphor" href="/methodology/">Methodology</a></li>
        <li><a class="text-paper hover:text-phosphor" href="/press/">Press kit</a></li>
        <li><a class="text-paper hover:text-phosphor" href="/changelog/">Changelog</a></li>
        <li><a class="text-paper hover:text-phosphor" href="/about/">About &amp; licensing</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-3 text-[0.8125rem] leading-relaxed text-dim">
      <p>
        <span class="term-label text-paper">Credits ·</span>
        Scores combine public datasets; every number links to its source on the{' '}
        <a class="text-paper underline" href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>. Exposure measures what AI can do to an
        occupation's tasks, not whether the job disappears.
      </p>
      <p data-attribution>
        <span class="term-label text-paper">Attribution ·</span>
        Employment projections and AI exposure categories: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics (public domain). Tasks and
        related occupations: O*NET 31.0 Database by the U.S. Department of Labor, Employment and Training Administration,
        used under CC BY 4.0. AI applicability scores: Microsoft Research, "Working with AI" (CC BY 4.0). Occupation
        exposure: OpenAI, "GPTs are GPTs" (MIT License). Type set in JetBrains Mono, IBM Plex Mono and Atkinson
        Hyperlegible (SIL Open Font License) via Google Fonts.
      </p>
      <p class="term-label text-[0.6875rem]">© {year} {SITE_NAME} · Gallows humor with receipts</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
